# Check everything out with LF on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. The `games/` corpus is embedded into the test
# binary with `include_str!` and then pattern-matched by fixtures that splice in
# deterministic starting state, e.g.
#
#     GAME.replace("  spawn_tile()\n  spawn_tile()", "  cells[0] = 2 …")
#
# Under a CRLF checkout the file contains "\r\n", the pattern never matches, and
# `replace` silently returns the text unchanged — so the test runs the *unmodified*
# game and fails somewhere far away ("first swipe scored incorrectly") with no
# hint that line endings were the cause. `corpus_is_lf_only` guards this too.
#
# The VM itself is indifferent: luax compiles CRLF and LF to identical assembly.
# What matters is that the embedded corpus is byte-identical everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
